    kl:action_type "CORRECTIVE" .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-CAVITATION> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Cavitation" ;
    kl:id "FM-CAVITATION" ;
    kl:severity "HIGH" ;
    kl:description "Vapour bubbles form at the impeller eye and collapse inside the impeller." ;
    kl:physics "When the absolute pressure at the impeller eye approaches the fluid's vapour pressure (NPSHa approaching NPSH3), vapour bubbles form and then collapse violently in higher-pressure regions. The implosions cause broadband vibration and noise, pit the vanes, and vapour blocking the passages breaks down the developed head and flow." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-BEARING> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Drive-end bearing degradation" ;
    kl:id "FM-BEARING" ;
    kl:severity "HIGH" ;
    kl:description "Rolling-element bearing distress (lubrication failure, contamination or fatigue)." ;
    kl:physics "Loss of the lubricant film, contamination or fatigue spalling increases rolling friction, raising bearing temperature; defects on races or rolling elements generate impacts that raise radial vibration. Higher temperature degrades the lubricant further, a self-accelerating loop." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-MISALIGNMENT> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Pump-motor shaft misalignment" ;
    kl:id "FM-MISALIGNMENT" ;
    kl:severity "MEDIUM" ;
    kl:description "Angular or parallel offset between pump and motor shafts." ;
    kl:physics "The coupling is forced to flex every revolution, producing cyclic reaction forces that are characteristically strong in the axial direction (1x and 2x running speed) and add load to the bearings, which raises bearing temperature." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-IMBALANCE> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Rotor / impeller imbalance" ;
    kl:id "FM-IMBALANCE" ;
    kl:severity "MEDIUM" ;
    kl:description "Mass centre of the rotor offset from its axis of rotation." ;
    kl:physics "The offset mass creates a centrifugal force F = m*e*omega^2 rotating at 1x running speed, giving predominantly radial vibration. Hydraulic performance (head, NPSH) is unaffected, which distinguishes imbalance from cavitation: while the NPSH margin is low, vibration cannot be attributed to imbalance." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-SEAL-LEAK> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Mechanical seal leakage" ;
    kl:id "FM-SEAL-LEAK" ;
    kl:severity "HIGH" ;
    kl:description "Process fluid escaping across the mechanical seal faces." ;
    kl:physics "The seal relies on a thin fluid film between rotating and stationary faces. Face wear, thermal distortion or heat-checking (e.g. after dry running) and elastomer degradation open the gap; leakage trips the leak detector and frictional heat raises the seal-chamber temperature." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-DRY-RUN> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Dry running (loss of suction)" ;
    kl:id "FM-DRY-RUN" ;
    kl:severity "CRITICAL" ;
    kl:description "The pump runs without liquid in the casing." ;
    kl:physics "Without liquid the impeller cannot develop head: discharge pressure collapses toward suction pressure and the head ratio falls to near zero. The motor only supplies mechanical losses, so current drops well below normal. The seal faces lose their lubricating and cooling film and overheat within minutes." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-DEADHEAD> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Deadheading (blocked discharge)" ;
    kl:id "FM-DEADHEAD" ;
    kl:severity "CRITICAL" ;
    kl:description "The pump runs against a closed or blocked discharge." ;
    kl:physics "The pump operates at shut-off: pressure rises to the shut-off head while flow is ~zero. For a radial centrifugal pump absorbed power is minimum at shut-off, so motor current FALLS (it does not rise). All absorbed power heats the trapped liquid, so seal-chamber temperature climbs and the liquid can eventually flash to vapour." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-IMPELLER-WEAR> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Hydraulic degradation (impeller / wear-ring wear)" ;
    kl:id "FM-IMPELLER-WEAR" ;
    kl:severity "MEDIUM" ;
    kl:description "Pump develops less head than its OEM curve at the same flow." ;
    kl:physics "Vane erosion and opened wear-ring clearances increase internal recirculation from discharge back to suction, so the pump develops less head than its curve at the measured flow (head ratio < 1). NPSH margin stays healthy and the motor stays loaded, which separates wear from cavitation and from loss of suction." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/FM-OVERLOAD> a kl:FailureMode ;
    rdfs:label "Motor overload" ;
    kl:id "FM-OVERLOAD" ;
    kl:severity "HIGH" ;
    kl:description "Motor draws more than its full-load current." ;
    kl:physics "Motor current tracks shaft load. For a radial centrifugal pump absorbed power rises with flow, so running far right on the curve (runout) overloads the motor; mechanical drag, a denser fluid or a low/unbalanced supply voltage do the same. The extra I^2R losses raise the winding temperature toward the insulation limit." .
<http://example.org/digitwin/instance/SYM%3Anpsh_margin%3ALOW> a kl:Symptom ;
    rdfs:label "NPSH margin ratio LOW" ;
    kl:id "SYM:npsh_margin:LOW" ;
